From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <bhoneycutt153@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: radv/android: recognize YV12 hardware buffers

YV12 is used by Android software video decoders. RADV returned an
undefined format and zero externalFormat for it, so ANGLE rejected the
EGLImage with EGL_BAD_PARAMETER. SurfaceFlinger then aborted while
mapping the frame in GaneshBackendTexture, restarting the Android UI.

Map YV12 to the three-plane Vulkan 4:2:0 format. The existing shared
vk_android_get_ahb_layout helper swaps the gralloc V/U offsets into
Vulkan U/V order and preserves each plane's stride.

Tested on the G14 Radeon 890M with CPU-written colour quadrants imported
through the system ANGLE driver: RGB, YV12 and flexible YUV420 all render
the expected pixels. The unpatched driver fails only the YV12 import.
---
diff --git i/src/amd/vulkan/radv_android.c w/src/amd/vulkan/radv_android.c
index 83bebec7b..a22379899 100644
--- i/src/amd/vulkan/radv_android.c
+++ w/src/amd/vulkan/radv_android.c
@@ -285,6 +285,11 @@ static inline VkFormat
 vk_format_from_android(unsigned android_format, unsigned android_usage)
 {
    switch (android_format) {
+   case AHARDWAREBUFFER_FORMAT_YV12:
+      /* vk_android_get_ahb_layout swaps the gralloc V/U plane layouts to
+       * Vulkan's U/V order, including the allocator's strides and offsets.
+       */
+      return VK_FORMAT_G8_B8_R8_3PLANE_420_UNORM;
    case AHARDWAREBUFFER_FORMAT_Y8Cb8Cr8_420:
       return VK_FORMAT_G8_B8R8_2PLANE_420_UNORM;
    case AHARDWAREBUFFER_FORMAT_IMPLEMENTATION_DEFINED:
